@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.product.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Product Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki product information transfers properly to the product index page.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prd.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRD                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prd.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRD                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korprd - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Prdkor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korprd - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| A Digital DXP Product     |
	| A Digital Portal Product  |
	| An Updated Portal Product |
	| Platinum Subscription     |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| PRDKORKORPRD |
	| PRDKOR       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korprd - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prdkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PRDKORKORPRD |
	| PRDKOR       |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Digital DXP Product     |
	| A Digital Portal Product  |
	| An Updated Portal Product |
	| Bronze Subscription       |
	| Copper Subscription       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korprd - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Prdkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korprd - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prdkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View products
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and viewing products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product |

Scenario: View updated product
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and viewing updated products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I update a product with the name "A Digital DXP Product" to have the following values
	| Name | A Digital Portal Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital Portal Product |
	And I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product"

Scenario: View deleted product
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and viewing deleted products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital DXP Product"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product"

Scenario: Create products
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Digital Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Bronze Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On              |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital Portal Product |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Bronze"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Bronze Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Bronze Subscription |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | A Digital Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                     | primary |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Bronze Subscription" and the following values
	| Name                    | Bronze Subscription |        |
	| Product Field and Value | type                | add-on |

Scenario: Create products with duplicate names
	Testing the ability to attempt to create products with names that already exist in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Digital DXP Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary               |
	Then I should be able to view the duplicate name error message on the product form containing the name "A Digital DXP Product"
	When I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Digital Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Platinum Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On                |
	Then I should be able to view the duplicate name error message on the product form containing the name "Platinum Subscription"
	When I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Bronze Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On              |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital Portal Product |
	And I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Bronze"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Bronze Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Bronze Subscription |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Platinum"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Platinum Subscription |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | A Digital Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                     | primary |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Bronze Subscription" and the following values
	| Name                    | Bronze Subscription |        |
	| Product Field and Value | type                | add-on |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Platinum Subscription | |

Scenario: Update products
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to update products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the product with the name "A Digital DXP Product" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Digital Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital Portal Product |
	And I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | A Digital Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                     | primary |

Scenario: Update created products
	Testing the ability to update products created in provisioning in the provisioning product index 

	Given I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Digital Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Bronze Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On              |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the product with the name "A Digital Portal Product" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | An Updated Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                   |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "Bronze"
	And I click on the product with the name "Bronze Subscription" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Copper Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On              |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "An"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "An Updated Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | An Updated Portal Product |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital Portal Product"
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Bronze"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Bronze Subscription"
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Copper"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Copper Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Copper Subscription |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "An Updated Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | An Updated Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                      | primary |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Copper Subscription" and the following values
	| Name                    | Copper Subscription |        |
	| Product Field and Value | type                | add-on |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital Portal Product"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Bronze Subscription"

Scenario: Update created products with duplicate names
	Testing the ability to update products created in provisioning with duplicate names in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Digital Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Bronze Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On              |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the product with the name "A Digital Portal Product" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | An Updated Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                   |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "Bronze"
	And I click on the product with the name "Bronze Subscription" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Platinum Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On                |
	Then I should be able to view the duplicate name error message on the product form containing the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Copper Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On              |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "An"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "An Updated Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | An Updated Portal Product |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product |
	And I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital Portal Product"
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Bronze"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Bronze Subscription"
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Copper"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Copper Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Copper Subscription |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Platinum"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Platinum Subscription |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "An Updated Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | An Updated Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                      | primary |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Copper Subscription" and the following values
	| Name                    | Copper Subscription |        |
	| Product Field and Value | type                | add-on |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Platinum Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Platinum Subscription | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital Portal Product"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Bronze Subscription"

Scenario: Delete products
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to update products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the delete button for the product "A Digital DXP Product"
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital DXP Product"

Scenario: Delete created products
	Testing the ability to update products created in provisioning in the provisioning product index 

	Given I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Digital Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the delete button for the product "A Digital Portal Product"
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should not be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital Portal Product"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital Portal Product"

Scenario: Delete products with purchases
	Testing the ability to delete products with purchases in the provisioning product index 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Digital DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera              |
	| Entity Id   | A Digital DXP Product |
	| Entity Name | product               |
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prdkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRD                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRD                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Digital DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korprd - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I generate the product ID value for "A Digital DXP Product" 
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the delete button for the product "A Digital DXP Product"
	Then I should be able to view the product purchase error message on the product index resulting from an attempted deletion of the product with the id value "${staticProductId}"
	When I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |

Scenario: Delete products with consumptions
	Testing the ability to delete products with consumptions in the provisioning product index 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |
	And I create an external link on a product "A Digital DXP Product" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera              |
	| Entity Id   | A Digital DXP Product |
	| Entity Name | product               |
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prdkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prd.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRD                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prd.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRD                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Digital DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korprd - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a product consumption for an account with the name "Korprd - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "A Digital DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1 | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2 | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3 | propertyValue3 |
	And I generate the product ID value for "A Digital DXP Product" 
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	And I click on the delete button for the product "A Digital DXP Product"
	Then I should be able to view the product consumption error message on the product index resulting from an attempted deletion of the product with the id value "${staticProductId}"
	When I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Digital DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Digital DXP Product | |